          type: 'Easy',
          explaination:
            "a) i) Not valid — the question is a double-barrelled question (asks about two things at once); it is unclear which subject the respondent is referring to. [1]\n   ii) Not reliable — ambiguous questions lead to inconsistent responses across different people or occasions. [1]\nb) i) Partially valid — it measures enjoyment but is vague; 'enjoyed' is subjective. [1]\n   ii) Not reliable — responses depend on mood at the time; results would vary if asked at a different time. [1]",
